au14-mast-untrained = You are not trained to work on this. Mast work requires engineering training.
au14-mast-examine-untrained = [color=gray]You need engineering training to work on this.[/color]

au14-mast-examine-unkeyed = [color=yellow]No COMSEC keys are loaded. The mast is not relaying anything.[/color]
au14-mast-examine-keyed = Keyed for: [color=cyan]{ $factions }[/color].
au14-mast-examine-feed-open = [color=orange]The feed panel is open.[/color] Use a COMSEC fill card to load a key, or a multitool to wipe them all. Screw and weld it shut to put the mast on the air.

au14-mast-condition-keyed = Load at least one COMSEC key before sealing the feed.
au14-mast-condition-keyed-guide = Load a COMSEC fill card into the feed

au14-mast-key-blank = That card has no key this mast can use.
au14-mast-key-already = The mast already has the { $faction } key loaded.
au14-mast-key-start = You start loading the key into the feed...
au14-mast-key-done = { $faction } key loaded.
au14-mast-zeroize-empty = There are no keys in the feed to wipe.
au14-mast-zeroize-start = You start wiping the keys from the feed...
au14-mast-zeroize-done = All keys wiped. The mast is blank.

au14-mast-site-underground = A mast needs open sky. There is too much rock overhead here.
au14-mast-site-roofed = A mast needs open sky and cannot be built under a roof. You pick the footing back up.
au14-mast-site-no-ground = There is no ground here to stake the footing into.
au14-mast-site-cramped = There is not enough room for the guy lines. Keep the tiles around the mast clear of walls.
au14-mast-site-crowded = Another mast or comms array is too close. They would interfere with each other.
